  "goodToKnow": "Der Damm is a dam or embankment: der Staudamm (dam across a river), der Bahndamm (railway embankment). Along coasts and rivers, Germans usually say der Deich. In Berlin, der Damm also appears in street names, like the famous Kurfürstendamm, often called der Ku'damm. The idiom nicht auf dem Damm sein means to feel under the weather. Einer Sache einen Damm entgegensetzen means to stem something. Plural: die Dämme."
